  "caption": "Quinn noticed one foot looking flatter, the inner ankle aching after long walks, and shoes worn down on the inside edge.\n\nA flattening arch in adults is often linked to an overloaded tibialis posterior tendon on the inside of the ankle. It's most common in people in their 40s to 60s, and early review tends to help.\n\nWhat can help: try a single-leg heel raise as a quick check, wear supportive shoes early on, build calf and tendon strength progressively over weeks, and avoid big spikes in standing or walking. Lifelong flexible flat feet often don't need treatment.\n\nGet it checked early if you have inner-ankle pain with a flattening arch, can't do a single-leg heel raise, or the foot keeps flattening.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
